{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the primary uncertainty is the overall performance floor and the relative contribution of each design axis (modality, profile type, encoder, aggregation, fusion). config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard RNA baseline: PCA is a fast, well-understood linear encoder and singleprofile removes the aggregation/fusion variables entirely. Running this first establishes a clear performance reference point. All subsequent experiments—image-only, multimodal, multiprofile, learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), and different aggregation/fusion strategies—can then be interpreted as deltas against this floor. Without this anchor, a multimodal result would be ambiguous (is it strong because of the combination or because one modality is already sufficient?). Under a limited budget, spending the first slot on the cleanest possible baseline maximizes the interpretability and information yield of every later experiment."
}

